<section class="section shell lifecycle" id="lifecycle">
  <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
    <span class="eyebrow">Inside one update</span>
    <h2>
      From changing edge
      <br />
      to a <span class="serif gradient-text">checked answer.</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      Axiom treats the matcher as one state boundary. The graph, matching,
      partner map, indexes, and hierarchy move together; a new snapshot is
      visible only after the invariant checks pass.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="lifecycle__steps">
    <li data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 0ms">
      <span class="lifecycle__number mono">01</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Accept the update</h3>
        <p>Validate the endpoints and operation, then apply the edge change inside the matcher’s atomic boundary.</p>
        <code>insert(u, v) · delete(u, v)</code>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
      <span class="lifecycle__number mono">02</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Repair the neighborhood</h3>
        <p>Update matching state and indexes, rematch affected vertices, and account for the work in the ledger.</p>
        <code>matching · partners · stats</code>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
      <span class="lifecycle__number mono">03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Check the invariant</h3>
        <p>Confirm that the matching remains valid and maximal before the new state is exposed to the caller.</p>
        <code>maximal() → True</code>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
      <span class="lifecycle__number mono">04</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Continue the stream</h3>
        <p>Keep the same matcher as the owner of graph state; persist the trace when the result needs to be replayed.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/examples/`}>See the update recipes&nbsp;→</a>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

